 "long_sentences": [
  [
   107,
   "The f4 bound is STATIC ONLY: the dynamic f4 arm has now been run (fresh per-arm af-matched bisects on the floor-4 graph, cut at the re-derived window \u2014 f4wA = first 20, f4ng = first 21 including the carrier, f4tw = first 20 plus the f4 mass-twin DNpe005-R; one batch, n = 16) and the registered R-side cliff does NOT transfer: all three f4 arms sit at kR 0/16 (meanR .043/.081/.082, upper bound .194) while the base-substrate arms reproduce on the SAME seeds (cutng25 SUPER 16/16 meanR .754, cutwA PARTIAL 3/16 .371), and the f4ng-vs-f4tw XOR leg is flat (\u2212.001 paired, 8 up / 8 down) [l169b2.dyn]."
  ],
  [
   77,
   "A census of every stored lineage trace quantifies the pattern: in the l65-baseline arm the global peak is sub-band in 449 of 449 UNIQUE SEEDS (Wilson lb .992) at a stable median .100 Hz that survives linear detrend in every case \u2014 a real slow oscillation rather than trend wander, but a stimulus-locked one (\u00a72.8) \u2014 while the intact closure is sub-band in 348 of 433 unique seeds (lb .764) with a less frequency-stable slow component [l172.census_unique]."
  ],
  [
   72,
   "A per-pool carrier census (two fresh batches, B33/B34) shows this line is not antagonist-clock-wide: the mm/xm aggregates carry it in 36 of 36 traces each, and a Tr/Ta/Sr subset of the antagonist pools in 8 of 20 (pooled Wilson lb \u2265 .56, subset median .100 Hz; strongest members 36/36), while the Ti pools stay at \u2264 6 of 36 and the strongest Pr pool reaches 20 of 36 (lb .396) [l157.pooled] (Fig."
  ],
  [
   68,
   "Under the strongest ADMISSIBLE floor (f4: keep pairs with \u2265 4 synapses, deleting 27.1% of closure edges, 647,953 \u2192 472,095 [l146.f4]) the CARRIER is robust \u2014 rank 25 \u2192 21 (inside the 19\u201329 window), 69/80 edges survive, heavy-cohort Jaccard .9231 \u2014 while the TWIN selection is floor-3-contingent (twin rank 26 \u2192 33, adjacency does not port): the identity claim and the twin-XOR selection have different data dependencies [l146.f4]."
  ],
  [
   66,
   "The Kopel-class caveat that does apply is about DETECTION rather than weight: in that preregistered screen, two of five criteria fail on BANC at a 2\u20133-synapse floor while the male and FlyWire volumes hold to thresholds of 10\u201315, and the stated cause is measurement \u2014 only 22% of BANC's detected synapses end on an identified neuron, against 41.9% and 40.1% in the other two volumes [12]."
  ],
  [
   65,
   "One post-hoc observation is reported without a claim: on the floored substrate the structure moves to the LEFT side (f4wA meanL .698, kL 16/16, versus .233 for base cutwA), where carrier removal COSTS structure (f4ng .289, paired \u2212.409, 16/16 seeds down) more than its mass-matched twin does (f4tw .560, paired \u2212.139) [l169b2.lat_descriptive]; a registered left-side test is queued and nothing in \u00a72 depends on it."
  ],
  [
   65,
   "- DATA FLOOR: the BANC v626 connections release carries an IMPLICIT pair-level synapse floor of 3 \u2014 all 2,676,592 pairs sum \u2265 3 (811,821 exactly at 3, zero below; the 574,733 one-synapse per-neuropil ROWS exist only as intra-pair breakdowns: 462,170 pairs contain such a row yet still sum \u2265 3) [l146.release] \u2014 so a single-synapse sensitivity critique has no purchase on this release's pair weights."
  ]
 ],
